    id:       'strata-css',
    category: 'PACKAGE',
    title:    'strata-css',
    meta:     'npm · MIT · Free',
    body: [
      'strata-css is a JIT CSS framework — Bootstrap-style ready-made components (`btn-primary`, `card`, `navbar`) alongside Tailwind-style arbitrary values (`mt-[24px]`, `bg-[#ff0000]`) and state variants (`hover:`, `focus-visible:`, `group-hover:`, `peer-checked:`, `before:`, `print:`), scanned and generated just-in-time so only used classes ship.',
      'Framework styles live inside CSS cascade layers, so nothing ever needs `!important`, and plain unlayered CSS automatically overrides it. Components are driven by `data-st-*` attributes rather than JavaScript class toggling, with built-in light, dark, and dim themes.',
      'Six companion packages extend it further: `@strata-packages/modal`, `offcanvas`, `picker`, `forms`, `chart`, and `shopmap` — each installable standalone. This exact site runs entirely on it; there is no other CSS framework loaded anywhere on these pages.',
    ],
    topics: ['The Package', 'The Companion Set', "It's Running Right Now"],
  },
  {
    id:       'triforge',
    category: 'PACKAGE',
    title:    '@triforge/*',
    meta:     'npm · MIT · 19 packages, Free',
    body: [
      'Triforge is a 19-package suite — `shader-core`, `geometry-nodes`, `particle-core`, `physics-core`, `keyframe`, and more — that brings Blender\'s node-graph workflow to plain Three.js, with Three.js as the only hard dependency.',
      'Every planet material, atmosphere, and ring on this site, plus the warp transition and the landing-page carousel, compiles from a Triforge node graph rather than hand-written GLSL. It works with vanilla Three.js and React Three Fiber on any r128+ project, with no required build step.',
      'Stage 1 — all 19 packages — shipped and is MIT-licensed. Stage 2, a GUI node-editor application and a terrain/vegetation addon suite, is the next milestone on the public roadmap.',
    ],
    topics: ['The Package', 'What It Powers Here', 'The Roadmap'],
  },
  {
    id:       'ai-dev-kit',
    category: 'PACKAGE',
    title:    'ai-dev-kit',
    meta:     'GitHub · MIT · Free',
    body: [
      'AI Dev Kit is a portable set of agent skills and layered coding standards for AI-assisted development — built for Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, and other agents that read markdown. It is not an npm package; it installs by copying markdown files into a project.',
      'Each skill lives in a single `SKILL.md` file that only loads when its trigger matches the task at hand, keeping an agent\'s context focused instead of front-loading every possible instruction. The coding-standards layer covers CSS, HTML, JS/TS, git, SEO, accessibility, and performance, with framework-specific overrides for Astro, Bootstrap, and Strata.',
      'A project-wide code-audit skill checks 47 script-checkable rules against a baseline so the violation count only moves down — the same discipline this portfolio\'s own codebase is held to.',
    ],
    topics: ['The Package', 'How Skills Load', 'The Audit Baseline'],
  },
];
